# What this project is responsible for, and what happens when it breaks.
level: 1
owner: Eli Ferres
monitor: GitHub Actions on every push and pull request; the badge in the README is the health signal. Failures surface as issues.
rollback: git revert, then re-tag. Installed copies are pinned to a version and are unaffected until the user upgrades.
migrations: n/a: the library owns no database and no schema.
backups: n/a: the library stores nothing. Text goes in, verdicts and rendered pieces come out, and nothing is written anywhere.
authz: n/a: no server and no trust boundary. It runs inside whatever program calls it, with exactly that program's permissions.
logs: n/a: a library and a command-line tool that print their findings and exit. The output is the log, and the caller decides where it goes.
alerts: n/a: nothing runs unattended. A non-zero exit from the command, or a refusal returned to the calling program, is how it raises its hand.
